            <profile id="5d42-64ea-6b08-c580" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, bow, and horse. May take shield (+2 pts). Vlachs may take thrusting spears (+2 pts). Skirmishers. Nomad Cavalry. Allies and Mercenaries. This entry represents the various types of light horse available to Serbian generals through the 14th and 15th centuries. (Vlad the Impaler p.71)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="e1f4-902d-4f7b-8e4d" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
