  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="2f2b-5788-fd85-0fc3" name="Serbia (Vlad the Impaler) - List Notes" publicationId="dab5-785d-be28-f228" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF SERBIA (Vlad the Impaler, pp.67-71): the Kingdom of Serbia (1280-1340), the Serbian Empire (1340-1371) and the Serb Despotates (1372-1459). Allies from other lists are documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Serbia - Kingdom of Serbia (1280-1340)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 40%, at least 20%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  KINGDOM OF SERBIA, 1280-1340. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry 20-40% (Vlastella are the only cavalry choice available at this time; a maximum of one lance armed unit may be taken for every bow and spear armed unit); Infantry up to 50% (2+ units of Strelac must be taken; Schiopetti may not be taken); Special Troops: 0-1 Mangonel may be taken for each full 1,000 points - no other special troops are available; Allies and Mercenaries up to 25% (European Mercenary Knights are limited to 0-1 in the first 2,000 points, and an additional 0-1 for every 1,000 points thereafter). Additionally, Serbia may take allies from Byzantines (Pronoia/Stratiotai, Kontaritoi, and Archers), Ottomans (Akinci representing Turcomans, or Tartars) and Walachians from 1330 (Calarasi or Lefegii) (documented only).
[Serbia - Serbian Empire (1340-1371)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  SERBIAN EMPIRE, 1340-1371. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry 25-50% (1+ unit of Vlastella must be taken per 1,000 points; a maximum of one bow and spear armed unit may be taken for every lance armed unit; all cavalry choices are available); Infantry up to 50% (Schiopetti may not be taken during this period); Special Troops: 0-1 Mangonels may be taken for each full 1,000 points - no other special troops are available; Allies and Mercenaries up to 25% (as the Kingdom of Serbia).
[Serbia - Serb Despotates (1372-1459)]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%, at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Special Units: up to 10%
  Allies and Mercenaries: up to 25%
  SERB DESPOTATES, 1372-1459. Characters up to 25%; Cavalry 25-50% (1+ unit of Vlastella - lance-armed variant only - must be taken per 1,000 points; all other cavalry choices are available); Infantry up to 50% (one unit of Schiopetti may be taken for every unit of Vojnici); Special Troops up to 10% (all choices are available; 0-1 Organ Gun); Allies and Mercenaries up to 25% (European Mercenary Knights are limited to 0-1 in the first 2,000 points, and an additional 0-1 for every 1,000 points thereafter). Additionally, Serbia may take allies from Albanians, Bulgars (until 1396), Ottomans (Akinci, Azab/Yaya, Balkan Tribal Warbands, Darabanci, and Tartars) and Walachians (Calarasi or Lefegii) (documented only).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
